    {
      "duration_ms": 11500,
      "caption": "A phi node at the join selects a value according to which predecessor the control came from.",
      "narration": "The fix is a phi node at the top of the join block. It yields x1 if control came from the then-block, and x2 from the else-block.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "h",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "The phi node",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 5,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "ir",
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "llvm",
          "text": "join:\n  %x3 = phi i32 [ %x1, %then ],\n                [ %x2, %else ]\n  ret i32 %x3",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 20,
          "w": 84,
          "enter": "slide-up",
          "at": 1300
        },
        {
          "id": "hl",
          "type": "highlight",
          "target": "ir",
          "at": 2100
        },
        {
          "id": "n",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "phi is not a real instruction: it is resolved when leaving SSA form.",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 50,
          "w": 84,
          "enter": "fade",
          "color": "orange",
          "at": 2900
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 10500,
      "caption": "Cytron's algorithm places phis at the iterated dominance frontier of each variable's definition blocks.",
      "narration": "Cytron's algorithm takes the blocks defining each variable, computes their iterated dominance frontier, and puts a phi at each. Then a dominator-tree walk renames uses.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "h",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Cytron placement",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 5,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "steps",
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "DF(n): blocks where n's dominance ends",
            "Put a phi at DF of every def block of v",
            "A phi is itself a def, so iterate: DF+",
            "Rename in a dominator-tree walk, one stack per variable"
          ],
          "x": 8,
          "y": 18,
          "w": 84,
          "enter": "slide-up",
          "color": "purple",
          "at": 1300
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 9500,
      "caption": "The result is minimal SSA; LLVM's mem2reg uses the same idea to promote allocas to registers.",
      "narration": "The result is minimal SSA. LLVM's mem2reg applies the same dominance-frontier idea to promote alloca stack slots into SSA values with phis.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "h",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "In LLVM",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 5,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "cmd",
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "text": "opt -passes=mem2reg -S in.ll",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 20,
          "w": 84,
          "enter": "slide-up",
          "at": 1300
        },
        {
          "id": "n",
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "alloca/load/store become SSA values",
            "phis appear only at dominance frontiers",
            "Pruned SSA also drops phis for dead vars"
          ],
          "x": 8,
          "y": 34,
          "w": 84,
          "enter": "slide-up",
          "color": "green",
          "at": 2100
        }
      ]
